hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27322","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, and Ishaq ibn Isa said: Malik informed me, Abdullah said: And Musab narrated to us, he said: Malik informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from Abd al-Rahman and Mujammi the two sons of Yazid ibn Jariya, from Khansa bint Khidham, that her father married her off while she was unwilling, and she was previously married, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled his marriage."
"27323","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, he said: al-Qasim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid and Mujammi, two shaykhs of the Ansar, that Khansa, her father gave her in marriage and she disliked that, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled it."
"27324","Abu Muawiya narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: He narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Mujammi ibn Yazid, from Umm Mujammi, he said: Khidam married off his daughter while she was unwilling, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father married me off while I am unwilling. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) annulled her father's marriage."
"27325","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid al-Ansari and Mujammi ibn Yazid al-Ansari informed him that a man among them called Khidham gave a daughter of his in marriage, and she disliked her father's marriage, so she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, so he annulled her father's marriage from her, then she married Abu Lubaba ibn Abd al-Mundhir. And Yahya mentioned that it reached him that she was previously married."
"27326","He said: I read to Yaqub ibn Ibrahim, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hajjaj ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Lubaba ibn Abd al-Mundhir al-Ansari narrated to me that his grandmother Umm al-Saib Khunas bint Khidham ibn Khalid was with a man before Abu Lubaba, she became widowed from him, then her father Khidham ibn Khalid married her to a man from Banu Amr ibn Awf ibn al-Khazraj, but she refused except to incline to Abu Lubaba, and her father refused except to bind her to the Awfi man, until her matter was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: She has more right to her affair, so join her to her desire. He said: So she was taken from the Awfi man, and she married Abu Lubaba, and she bore him Abu al-Saib ibn Abi Lubaba."
"27327","He said: I read to my father: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Saib ibn Abi Lubaba, he said: Khunas bint Khidham was with a man, she became widowed from him, then her father married her to a man from Banu Awf, while she inclined to Abu Lubaba. Her father refused except to bind her to the Awfi man, and she refused, until their case was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he said: She has more right to her affair, so join her to her desire. So she married Abu Lubaba, and she bore him Abu al-Saib."
